      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Was my message edited? because I know it was bigger than this because I saved a copy of it right before sending it.\n\nThe new UI is not easier to glance at in even the slightest. Accounts without VRC+ showed the images for their avatars, which for moderators made it easier to quickly glance at accounts that wore strange avatars or known trolls/crashers who re-used the same image on their avatars. As well as trolls/crashers who are part of a group that wear matching avatars. Same thing with groups or statuses, which are now basically hidden. Offline users should still show their status for crashers who crash themselves. Kick/ban buttons were RIGHT there at the bottom of your screen for ease of use. Now there's an extra (very small) button that you have to click first, and the kick/ban buttons themselves are very small. This makes it harder for staff to kick users who are being a nuisance. They could be placed at the bottom or top of the screen but not behind ANOTHER button. Before, you could see a user's bio, profile pictures, groups, badges, language, and notes all at once without having to scroll around like you do now. Things are stupidly big in size now, and there's so much empty space on profiles. Maybe it would be better if it faded out into the menu instead.\n\nHere is the beginning of my message^ that has somehow been taken out now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-24T23:16:10.701Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Why is the \"gift VRC+\" button at the top in bright yellow and bigger than more important buttons like the report button? Why is the \"give me your money\" button more important than the report button? Also, there's no longer an avatar button on people's profiles anymore. You used to be able to open a person's profile and open their avatar without having to actually turn on and load the user's profile. \"Ah, this fella looks like he's in a crasher avi; let me check the info on his avi to find out. \"Well, if you want to know now, you have to take the chance of crashing yourself. The UI on the VRC website works because the website takes up your entire screen. While the UI in game has a little menu to fill. Profile effects are just another thing users have to load, and another thing you have to spend money on. The old menu was much more compact and actually appealing to look at. Also bring back the yellow friend tact instead of a big bubble around the person's name. \n\nEnough ranting. I made a little doodle for what some of these things could look like.\n\nUsing compact icons below the name look much better than the stupidly big icons we have now. You get all the info you need on a user without it taking up a quarter of your screen.",
